-- title:
--   Global ideal of an ideal sheaf pulled back along Specφ
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ and $B$ be commutative rings (in a fixed universe), let $\varphi : A \to B$ be a ring homomorphism, and let $I$ be an ideal sheaf datum on the affine scheme $\operatorname{Spec} A$, i.e. a coherent assignment of an ideal $I(U) \subseteq \Gamma(\operatorname{Spec} A, U)$ to each affine open $U$. Write $\operatorname{Spec}(\varphi) : \operatorname{Spec} B \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ for the induced morphism of schemes and let $I.\mathrm{comap}\,\operatorname{Spec}(\varphi)$ be the pullback of $I$ along it. The assertion is an equality of two ideals of $B$: the image, under the canonical isomorphism $\Gamma(\operatorname{Spec} B, \top) \cong B$ given by `Scheme.ΓSpecIso`, of the ideal that $I.\mathrm{comap}\,\operatorname{Spec}(\varphi)$ attaches to the affine open $\top$ of $\operatorname{Spec} B$, coincides with the ideal of $B$ generated by $\varphi$ of the image, under $\Gamma(\operatorname{Spec} A, \top) \cong A$, of the ideal that $I$ attaches to the affine open $\top$ of $\operatorname{Spec} A$. In other words, if $J \subseteq A$ is the global ideal of $I$, then the global ideal of the pulled-back ideal sheaf is the extension $\varphi(J)\cdot B$.
--
--   This records, in the language of Mathlib's ideal sheaf data, the elementary fact that on affine schemes the closed-subscheme pullback corresponds to ideal extension of scalars: reading the pullback of an ideal sheaf on global sections gives the extended ideal. It is used in the construction of global Drinfeld-type level structures, where ideals cut out by torsion conditions on a Weierstrass model must be compared after base change, via [`WeierstrassCurve.DrinfeldGlobal.map_ideal_comap_ker_one_eq_span`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.DrinfeldGlobal.map_ideal_comap_ker_one_eq_span) and [`WeierstrassCurve.DrinfeldGlobal.map_ideal_comap_torsionIdeal_eq_span_nthSeries`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.DrinfeldGlobal.map_ideal_comap_torsionIdeal_eq_span_nthSeries).
